{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 2, :comments ["<b>Eleven days from Horev, etc.</b> This is because all thirty-eight years that He moved them about in the wilderness, hither and thither, they did not travel on a straight path directed toward a known destination. And when they would arrive at a place from which they would set out and turn back behind them or to the sides and not on a straight path, Moses would say to them: See what you have caused — for it is a journey of eleven days from Horev to Kadesh Barnea by way of Mount Seir, which is the shortest route for travelers. And the blessed El led you to Kadesh Barnea in three days by way of the great and awesome wilderness, yet because of your sin you wander all this time. And all this he said so that they would remember and return to HaShem."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :sforno, :lang :en, :chapter 1, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T16:20:03.383670345Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}